SUMMARY:Fitness Hike: MST to the Bear Trail.
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n* Out and back 3.5-4 hour Hike wil
 l begin at the Folk Arts Center on the MST North direction for 2 1/2 miles
  past the major climb and decent to a right on a spur trail leading to the
  Bear trail. The Bear trail is new and only partly scouted. We will hike i
 n the outbound direction for approximetly 1.75 hours with a snack before r
 eturning. Elevation data and distance are estimates. The scouted part of t
 he Bear trail was relatively smooth with minimal rocks and in good conditi
 on. The hike is mostly under a forest canopy and has a rural-back country 
 feel.\n* **Length** ? aproximately 10-11 miles.\n* **Elevation gain estima
 te:** in the mid-level range (1800 +/-. feet.\n* **PACE:** Brisk pace of 2
 .5 mph on steeper climbs or rugged trail condition to 3-3+ mph on lesser c
 limbs and downhill sections.\n* **Dogs: Trail friendly dogs welcome.**\n* 
 **WEATHER:**\nCheck for weather cancelation message on or before 7:30 AM i
 f the forecast is >50% chance of precipitation.\n* **Release of Liability 
 :**\nThe organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guid
 e. The function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sig
 n up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and volu
 ntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages ar
 ising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In addition\
 , you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.c
 om/terms
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/313851320
 /
