UID:event_314460912@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260428T035241Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T123000
SUMMARY:Craven Gap Out-and-Back -- 5 mi\, 800 ft. elev. gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[Sign ups open Sunday\, April 26
 th\, 8:00 PM]**\n\nThis segment of the Mountain-to-Sea Trail was devastate
 d by Hurricane Helene and closed for well over a year. But now it's back! 
 If you're familiar with this hike\, the first mile was radically altered. 
 After that\, it looks a little more "normal."\n\nFrom the Craven Gap parki
 ng lot\, we cross the Parkway and head south on the Mountain-to-Sea Trail.
  It's hilly but doesn't add up to much elevation gain. We'll take a short 
 break 2.5 miles out\, then return the way we came. It's more scenic than i
 n the past due to lots of new vistas that used to be blocked by trees. Oth
 erwise\, just your basic\, beautiful\, winding forest trail. At our pace (
 about 2.4 mph)\, I'd give it a 3.5/10 difficulty rating. We should be back
  in the parking lot soon after noon.\n\nWell-behaved dogs are welcome\, bu
 t Forestry Service regulations require leashes.\n\n**\\*\\*\\* CARPOOLING 
 STRONGLY RECOMMENDED \\*\\*\\***\nThe Craven Gap parking lot used to be la
 rge\, but now it's small due to reconstruction. Please try to work out car
 pooling with others on the hike. Depending on where you're coming from\, g
 ood places to rendezvous may be (1) Ingles on Tunnel Rd. (closest to the d
 owntown tunnel)\, which is near Town Mountain Rd.\, (2) Harris-Teeter on M
 errimon Ave next to Trader Joe's\, (3) Folk Art Center. I'll be happy to b
 ring several people from my downtown location.\n\n**MEETING TIME AND PLACE
 **\n\nClick here for the [location on Google Maps](https://bit.ly/416noPy)
 . Better yet\, search for the **intersection of the Blue Ridge Parkway and
  Town Mountain Road**. From the intersection of College St. & Town Mtn. Rd
 . in downtown Asheville\, the Craven Gap parking lot is 6.3 miles northeas
 t on Town Mtn. Rd.\n\nWe'll meet at **9:00 AM\,** so shoot for an 8:50 arr
 ival. After formalities and intros\, we'll set out by 9:05.\n\n**GUESTS**\
 n\nIf you'd like to bring a guest\, please have them join the Asheville Hi
 king Group and sign up for the hike independently.\n\n**COURTESY TO WAITLI
 STERS (Please!!)**\n\nOnly sign up if you \\*truly\\* plan to come. If you
  must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as soon as possibl
 e. Avoid dropping out within 18 hours of the hike so wait-listers can have
  sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a no-show.\n\nWe'll 
 watch the weather and post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM on the mornin
 g of the hike if the forecast is >50% chance of precipitation.\n\n\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**LEGA
 LESE**\n\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly
 \, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsibl
 e for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, 
 physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks
  to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking
  Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume
  full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314460912
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260424T174256Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260424T174256Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
