SUMMARY:Maxwell\, Pressley Cove(s) loop
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nN.B. will be watching the weather 
 forecast\, and if need be will just roll the hike into Sunday for those wh
 o have that flexibility (if it happens)\n\nthis is about a 5 mile (maybe a
  bit less) loop with 1000-ish feet of elevation gain in the ranger station
  section of Pisgah.\n\nthe starting point is the newer gravel parking lot 
 near Avery creek about 1.6 miles in on the forest service road leading to 
 the stables\, Twin Falls etc. just past the Bennett Gap trail. carpooling 
 is encouraged\n\nfrom the starting point\, ascent to Maxwell Cove is via a
 n unmarked trail further down the road\, with an approx 1 mile climb. We t
 hen wend our way up Maxwell\, past an interesting historical ruin to Press
 ley Gap\, where the Black Mountain trail crosses. Then back down Maxwell t
 o Pressley Cove trail\, which leads back down to the parking area.\n\nwell
  behaved dogs are welcome on this hike\n\nsay 2 - 2.5 mph pace\n\ngear up 
 as appropriate\, trekking poles are an option. bring a snack as we'll take
  a break mid-hike. and plenty of water\n\nground rules:\n\nif you sign up\
 , show up or change your status. a no-show may undercut a motivated wait-l
 ister. (repeated no-shows will have consequences) likewise\, if you're on 
 the wait list at the time of the hike\, don't presume to just show up\n\n2
  ) be sure you are in adequate physical shape to complete the event\n\n3) 
 show consideration. emphasize group effort and group cohesion. I hike for 
 stress reduction and want to keep it that way.\n\nLEGALESE\nThis Asheville
  Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and
  from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own safety a
 nd affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, 
 equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property
 . Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your s
 afety nor eliminate all risks. By signing up for this event\, participant 
 understands and agrees
